{"kind":"stack","id":"fossils-1","title":"How fossils are formed","theme":{"background":"#f4efe4","foreground":"#2b2b2b","font":"Georgia, serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"bulb"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-term","content":"Fossil"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-def","content":"The remains or traces of a plant or animal that lived long ago, kept in rock."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-term","content":"Sediment"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-def","content":"Small bits of sand, mud or dead material that settle in layers at the bottom of rivers, lakes and seas."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"What is a fossil?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"The remains or traces of something that lived long ago","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"A rock that is made from melted metal","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"A type of sand found only in deserts","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"river"},{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Where does sediment usually settle to form layers?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"At the bottom of rivers, lakes and seas","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"On the tops of tall mountains","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Inside clouds high in the sky","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-d","label":"Deep inside volcanoes","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"A dead fish sinks to the bottom of a lake. What should happen next?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Mud and sand cover it slowly","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"It floats away on the wind","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Layers of mud and sand harden over thousands of years. The fish leaves its shape in the rock."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"With nothing to cover it, the fish rots away completely. No trace is left behind."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"fish"},{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Why do most fossils form in sedimentary rock?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Sediment settles in layers that can trap and preserve remains","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Hot liquid rock cools and hides every living thing","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Wind blows animals into cracks in the ground","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which is bigger: a fossil of a dinosaur, or the rock it is trapped in?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"The rock","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"The fossil","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"clock"},{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"About how long does it take for a fossil to form?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Several days","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Thousands to millions of years","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"About one hour","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-d","label":"Exactly one year","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done: you finished the fossil lesson!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Fossils tell us about living things from long ago. Keep looking at rocks and wondering what they hide."}],"actions":[]}}
